// The `want` matrices below were produced by the node `qrcode` package (MIT,
// based on Kazuhiko Arase's reference encoder) for the same text, version and
// mask. Every fixture is lowercase-only so that the reference encodes it as a
// single byte segment, which is what this encoder does; a string it would split
// into numeric/alphanumeric runs is a different, shorter symbol by design.
//
// Fixtures marked with mask = -1 pin the mask *choice*: they are the symbols
// the reference picked when it was free to choose, so a change in the penalty
// scoring shows up here as well as a change in the bits.
Fixture :: struct {
	text:    string,
	mask:    int,
	version: int,
	want:    string,
}

